1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,688
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:31,156
[Ivy] <i>It's true! I am</i>
<i>the traitor in your family!</i>

6
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:36,870
<i>I, Ivy Aguas, am the traitor</i>
<i>in the Ardiente family!</i>

7
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:38,580
<i>Ivy Aguas is on our side.</i>

8
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:42,792
<i>She is the heart, mind,</i>
<i>and soul of our cause.</i>

9
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:44,377
[Julio] <i>Miss Aguas!</i>

10
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,045
<i>You can't escape now.</i>

11
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:50,508
<i>We set the trap,</i>
<i>and you jumped right into it.</i>

12
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:52,093
<i>You really are a traitor.</i>

13
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>And we were right all along.</i>

14
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:59,893
<i>Now, no snake will leave this place alive.</i>

15
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:02,896
<i>Don't celebrate just yet</i>

16
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:05,648
<i>because I'm not through with you!</i>

17
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,318
<i>If Lily really were fine,</i>
<i>she would've called ages ago.</i>

18
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:11,362
[Anna] <i>What's our next move against Julio?</i>

19
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,531
-[gunshot]
-[Pandoy] <i>He's pretty tough.</i>

20
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,575
<i>He's like a fearless action star.</i>
<i>Just like you.</i>

21
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:19,120
<i>He's the man we need</i>
<i>to take down the Ardientes.</i>

22
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:20,330
[Jepoy] <i>All that matters to me</i>

23
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,957
<i>is killing Julio Ardiente and Jaguar</i>

24
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,667
<i>so I can protect the ones I love.</i>

25
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:29,881
<i>If you want her, go ahead.</i>
<i>You can have her.</i>

26
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:35,720
<i>I want Arnaldo to see that woman die.</i>

27
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,722
[Emilia] <i>It's a done deal.</i>

28
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,265
<i>I shall see you, then. </i>[laughing]

29
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,059
<i>This is it.</i>

30
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:49,442
[phone ringing]

31
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:52,737
[Raul] <i>Diego.</i>

32
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:54,322
Dad?

33
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,700
Why did you call, son?

34
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:00,578
Dad, I'm sorry, but there's
no one else I can turn to.

35
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,580
I need your help.

36
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:04,249
What is it?

37
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:06,334
Just say the word and I'll help you.

38
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,253
Dad, Ivy's missing.

39
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:09,963
Do you have any idea where she is?

40
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,256
The last thing we know

41
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,882
is that she was
on her way to the Ardientes'.

42
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,509
<i>Dad, please, help us.</i>

43
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:16,052
We can't find Ivy.

44
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:20,056
I'm here at the mansion,
but she isn't here.

45
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,891
<i>Why? Is something wrong?</i>

46
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:23,685
I have a feeling
they've done something to her.

47
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:29,524
Hold on. Why are you
so worried about Ivy Aguas?

48
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:31,442
<i>Isn't she your enemy?</i>

49
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:32,902
She's on Julio's side.

50
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,363
Dad, Ivy is important to me.

51
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,326
Okay, I'll help you.

52
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:43,705
I'll see if they have anything
to do with her disappearance.

53
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,248
Thank you.

54
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:47,458
Thank you, Dad.

55
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:50,712
[unsettling music playing]

56
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,176
Diego, why did you call your father?

57
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,887
Anna, I'm desperate.

58
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:01,264
We have to know where Ivy is.

59
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:04,142
Your father is connected
to Julio and Emilia.

60
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:06,811
What if he tells them
you're in touch with Lily?

61
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,938
You'll be putting her life in danger.

62
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:10,440
Wake up, Anna.

63
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:12,442
Ivy's life has always been in danger.

64
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:15,445
So, I don't care if they
discover her identity anymore.

65
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:17,739
We have to do something now
because if we don't,

66
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,657
we might never see her alive.

67
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:22,493
[unsettling music playing]

68
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:29,250
Thank you.

69
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,419
Oh, there they are. Hello, Papa.

70
00:03:31,502 --> 00:03:33,296
[Julio] Hello, Emilia, my dear.

71
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:34,714
Oh, my son, Arnaldo.

72
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:36,424
-Welcome.
-Yes, I brought him along.

73
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,343
[Emilia chuckles] It's gonna be exciting.

74
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:39,510
Uh…

75
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:43,223
Interesting choice of location.

76
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:45,767
What do you have in store for us?

77
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,645
[laughs] Papa, you're gonna love this.

78
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:55,693
Today marks the death of Miss Ivy Aguas.

79
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:00,114
-[Emilia squeals]
-Is she really dying today?

80
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,034
-Yes, Papa.
-Oh, my. I don't believe this.

81
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,160
You monsters.

82
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:06,621
You're worse than the devil himself!

83
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:08,248
You're all monsters!

84
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:10,083
Shh! Quiet. Quiet. Quiet.

85
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:10,959
You witch!

86
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:12,543
I'm going to give you your last blessing,

87
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,003
so you should shut up.

88
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:16,130
Come on, let us all pray.

89
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:18,967
[grunts]

90
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:22,720
[Emilia] We are gathered here

91
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:27,600
for the soul of our friend, Ivy Aguas,

92
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,812
who's gonna be in a
better place than any of us.

93
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:39,028
In a place where she will stay
forever and ever in…

94
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,489
…hell! [laughs]

95
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:44,575
Oh. Finally.

96
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:45,660
[Emilia] There you go.

97
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:46,869
Put her in the coffin.

98
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,872
Colonel, would you like to help them?

99
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,250
You're finally going to die.

100
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,876
You bastards! What are you gonna do?

101
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,086
Let go of me!

102
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:59,590
Hey! You bastards! Let go of me!

103
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,968
-[Emilia laughs]
-What are you going to do?!

104
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:03,761
-Goodbye, Miss Aguas.
-Let me go!

105
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:06,055
What are you doing, huh?!

106
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,599
-Get off!
-[Emilia laughing]

107
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:10,685
-[Julio] She is feisty.
-[Emilia] Oh.

108
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:12,145
[Julio] Up to her last breath,

109
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:14,147
-she's feisty.
-I know, Papa.

110
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:15,940
You're monsters!

111
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,526
[Emilia] Papa, wait! Papa! Please!

112
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:22,155
Damn you, Emilia! You witch!

113
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:25,158
-Oh, please! No!
-You witch!

114
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:31,164
[Ivy screaming] You witch!

115
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:34,000
She's going to die now. Oh!

116
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:35,918
[Ivy] Damn you, Emilia!

117
00:05:37,128 --> 00:05:39,589
[fake crying]

118
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:42,216
[hysterical laugh]

119
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:50,058
Monsters! Damn you, Ardientes!

120
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:52,935
-Oh, come, come, come.
-[Ivy] I hate you, Emilia!

121
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,896
[Ivy] Curse you! Go to hell!

122
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:57,732
-[Emilia fake crying]
-[Ivy] You'll pay for this!

123
00:05:57,815 --> 00:06:02,153
You better get ready
because I'll have my revenge!

124
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:03,738
Please don't leave me, Ivy.

125
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:06,532
Please! [fake crying]

126
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:11,079
You think this is the last of me?!

127
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:16,584
It doesn't end here! You bastards!

128
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:19,796
-[Emilia laughs hysterically]
-Get this over with.

129
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:23,883
[fake crying] Ivy!

130
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:26,803
I'm gonna miss you, I swear.

131
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,264
[fake crying]

132
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,266
Don't! Don't! Don't! Don't!

133
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,435
Don't stop. Go on.

134
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:37,480
[laughs hysterically]

135
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:40,024
[grunts]

136
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:46,531
[Emilia laughs hysterically]

137
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:50,785
[grunting and panting heavily]

138
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:59,127
-[Ivy] No, please!
-[Julio] I see it.

139
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:02,130
But it's like I can't believe it.

140
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,508
She really is going to get buried.

141
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:08,052
[ominous music playing]

142
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,474
-[fire blazing]
-[people crying]

143
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,562
[grunts]

144
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,483
<i>Adios</i>, Ivy Aguas.

145
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:23,860
[whimpers]

146
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,946
[Emilia] Oh, Ivy.

147
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:37,290
May you rest in peace, and
bless your unfortunate soul.

148
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:41,377
-We will miss you.
-[lighter clicks]

149
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,047
[panting heavily]

150
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:49,051
[breathing raggedly] You damn Ardientes!

151
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:53,347
[tense music playing]

152
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:04,025
You bastards!

153
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:06,444
[sobbing]

154
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:09,989
You monsters! I hate you all!

155
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:13,743
Curse you, damn Ardientes!

156
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:15,912
Curse you!

157
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:18,831
[Ivy] <i>You'll all to hell!</i>

158
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,834
<i>I hate you all!</i>

159
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:27,465
[Ivy crying] <i>You are monsters!</i>
<i>Go to hell, Ardientes!</i>

160
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:29,675
<i>Damn you!</i>

161
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:33,513
Damn you!

162
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:35,890
[sobbing]

163
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:38,559
[tense music continues]

164
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:52,031
May you rest in peace, Ivy Aguas.

165
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,159
Can you please help me?

166
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:56,536
You're so slow.

167
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,579
My heels! Ouch!

168
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,249
[bangs on wood, grunting]

169
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:03,960
[tense music playing]

170
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:08,172
[clapping]

171
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:16,430
Emilia, you have
outdone yourself this time.

172
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:20,685
You have proven yourself
beyond all my imagination.

173
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:24,939
Truly, you have Ardiente blood
running in your veins.

174
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:29,443
And now, that this whole brouhaha is over,

175
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:33,864
we can focus our attention
on the centennial celebration

176
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:36,033
of the founding day of my…

177
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,663
I mean, of <i>our</i> province.

178
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:42,832
-[Emilia sighs]
-[Julio] Poblacion Ardiente.

179
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:44,333
Yes! [claps]

180
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,252
Papa, it's so exciting.

181
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:48,337
Quadruple celebration!

182
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:51,799
First, because you were elected governor.

183
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:56,554
Second, because I've been acquitted
of all my charges.

184
00:09:57,346 --> 00:10:02,602
Third, because Ivy Aguas
is finally laid to rest.

185
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:04,562
And fourth, because we're celebrating

186
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:07,857
our province's 100th year, Papa!

187
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:10,651
-A quadruple celebration!
-Yes! [laughs]

188
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:13,029
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

189
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:14,947
-Viva Ardiente!
-Life is so good!

190
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:17,158
Papa, it's so good.

191
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:19,201
Hashtag, "blessed".

192
00:10:20,536 --> 00:10:24,123
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

193
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:25,541
[laughs]

194
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,960
Goodbye, Ivy Aguas!

195
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:30,796
[tense music playing]

196
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:35,676
[grunting]

197
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,304
[breathing raggedly]

198
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:41,849
[solemn music playing]

199
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,020
[bangs]

200
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,563
[breathing raggedly]

201
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:02,870
[breathing raggedly]

202
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:04,664
[banging and crying]

203
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,749
You monsters!

204
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,712
Damn you, Ardientes!

205
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:14,632
Curse you!

206
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:17,510
Damn you!

207
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:20,721
[solemn music continues]

208
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,681
[sniffles]

209
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,104
[bangs]

210
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:34,944
Ivy.

211
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:39,657
You have five hours.

212
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:46,497
That's the longest
you can survive in here.

213
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,335
Ivy, you can still get out.

214
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:56,382
If Emilia and the rest
of the Ardientes think

215
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:58,551
you can't get out of here,

216
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:02,054
Ivy, they're wrong.

217
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:06,183
They're dead wrong.
I will get out of here!

218
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:09,770
I know it. I will get out of here, Emilia.

219
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:12,481
You will get out of here, Ivy!

220
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:17,445
[thunder rumbling]

221
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,657
What the--

222
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,285
[solemn music playing]

223
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:28,581
[thunder rumbling]

224
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:31,750
-[Emilia squeals]
-[Julio] Let's go!

225
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,544
[Emilia] It's raining.

226
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:34,670
Damn it!

227
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:40,718
-[Emilia exclaims]
-Let's go!

228
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:58,861
[banging and crying]

229
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:03,324
-[Lily] <i>Monsters!</i>
-[banging continues]

230
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,451
[Ivy] <i>You monsters!</i>

231
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:13,417
I need the revised program
by noon tomorrow, Kelly.

232
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:14,543
[snickers]

233
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:17,254
Remember, this is an important day

234
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,923
for Poblacion Ardiente.

235
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:21,926
This is our centennial celebration.

236
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:25,804
And this is our opportunity
to show the Philippines

237
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:30,309
that this province still belongs to us.

238
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:32,269
-[chuckles]
-Clear?

239
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:34,313
[Emilia snickers]

240
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:37,399
Emilia, are you with us?

241
00:13:38,692 --> 00:13:39,944
Yes, Papa, I am.

242
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:45,032
You seem to be in too much
of a good mood today.

243
00:13:45,115 --> 00:13:48,744
I've noticed you were
just smiling the whole time.

244
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:51,372
That's not it, Papa.

245
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:53,749
I'm just thinking that
the centennial celebration

246
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:57,461
should be exciting and fun
with all the fireworks!

247
00:13:58,003 --> 00:13:59,797
Why would you let the people endure

248
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:04,051
your long boring speeches, Papa?

249
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:08,681
Listen, Emilia,

250
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:13,060
if you have nothing good
to contribute to this program,

251
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:14,395
there's the door. Get out!

252
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:15,604
Get out! Get out!

253
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,022
Get out!

254
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:20,192
[Emilia] Wow, why is this
old man so irritable?

255
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:21,777
What did you say?

256
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,320
Huh?

257
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,490
Nothing.

258
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:31,036
[Emilia laughs] It's just boring speeches.

259
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:38,377
-[door closes]
-I have a nut for a daughter.

260
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,505
[tense music playing]

261
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,975
-[grunts]
-[soft thud]

262
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:10,451
[cloth rips]

263
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,419
[unsettling music playing]

264
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,049
[grunts]

265
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,856
[cloth ripping]

266
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:44,526
[grunts]

267
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:49,156
[tense music playing]

268
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:51,533
[man] <i>One-two, three-four.</i>

269
00:15:57,331 --> 00:15:59,249
[bangs loudly]

270
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:02,962
Help! Help!

271
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,922
-Five, six, seven, eight!
-<i>Help! Help!</i>

272
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:09,051
Eight, seven, six, five,
four, three, two, and one.

273
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:11,095
One, two, three, four…

274
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:13,681
[bangs] Help me!

275
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:15,265
<i>Help!</i>

276
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,518
Hey! Did you guys hear that?

277
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:20,354
Help! I'm trapped here!

278
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:22,231
Somebody help me!

279
00:16:22,314 --> 00:16:24,316
<i>-I'm trapped here!</i>
-There!

280
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,442
<i>Help!</i>

281
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:27,403
-Ghost!
-[screams]

282
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:34,243
[banging and sobbing]

283
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:38,372
Help! Please help me!

284
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:39,581
Help!

285
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:41,250
[cocks firearm]

286
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:47,214
Looks like somebody is
having fun with his new toys.

287
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:51,468
Don't worry, there's more
where that came from.

288
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,971
We're going to need more than guns and men

289
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,306
if we really want
to take down the Ardientes.

290
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,599
I know.

291
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:01,061
Don't worry, help will come soon.

292
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:04,940
[phone ringing]

293
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,654
Just a minute, ma'am.

294
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:17,161
-Hello?
-Jepoy, get over here now.

295
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,412
We need you.

296
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,205
Why, Anna? What's the problem?

297
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:22,041
Lily's still missing.

298
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,835
[tense music playing]

299
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,172
Ma'am, I have to go.

300
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,590
Where are you going?

301
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:31,884
I have to take care of something.

302
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,011
Lily Cruz…

303
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:35,971
and the gang?

304
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,891
The good guys? [scoffs]

305
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:40,434
I can't stand them.

306
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:43,062
They're so annoying.

307
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:48,400
Ma'am, I just have to handle this.

308
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,320
Madrigal.

309
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:56,408
I don't like sharing
my friends with others.

310
00:17:58,035 --> 00:18:00,621
And I don't like sharing you.

311
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:07,836
The day will come
when you'll have to choose…

312
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:11,048
where your loyalties lie.

313
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:13,342
With your friends?

314
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,803
[tense music playing]

315
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,263
Or with me?

316
00:18:20,015 --> 00:18:23,352
Them or me?

317
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:27,147
[tense music continues]

318
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:40,911
[door opens and closes]

319
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:47,167
Jaguar, my favorite cat, how are you?

320
00:18:47,918 --> 00:18:49,795
You sound too happy, Emilia.

321
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:52,589
No. I just miss you, Jaguar.

322
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:54,466
-Hmm.
-[chuckles]

323
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,135
How are you? It's been a long time.

324
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:57,970
And you are right.

325
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,055
I'm actually savoring the moment.

326
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:03,267
And I'm very, very happy
enjoying every minute of it.

327
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,769
I mean, you know what
I've been through, right?

328
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:07,646
I basically hit rock bottom,

329
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:11,567
but here I am now,
flying through the clouds.

330
00:19:12,192 --> 00:19:15,571
And maybe you'd like to guess
how I did that.

331
00:19:16,655 --> 00:19:17,781
How, Emilia?

332
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:19,533
Hmm…

333
00:19:19,616 --> 00:19:23,287
I caught the traitor in our family.

334
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,831
It's Ivy Aguas.

335
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:28,917
-Ivy Aguas?
-Mm-hm.

336
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:31,461
What did you do when you found out?

337
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:34,464
Secret. [chuckles]

338
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:36,175
Wait. Hold on, Jaguar.

339
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:37,467
We need to celebrate.

340
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:38,969
Aren't you even going to, like,

341
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:41,430
invite me for a drink or something?

342
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:43,432
We should be happy, right?

343
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,769
-I'll get you some wine.
-Thank you.

344
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:50,397
[ominous music playing]

345
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:59,239
[phone alarm ringing]

346
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,324
Hmm?

347
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:01,950
Whoops.

348
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:07,456
It's time to make that
very important call.

349
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:08,540
Okay.

350
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:13,545
[solemn music playing]

351
00:20:32,981 --> 00:20:38,779
[phone ringing]

352
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:55,963
[phone continues ringing]

353
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:59,132
Hello?

354
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:01,593
Hello, my evil "frenemy."

355
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,428
How are you?

356
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:06,139
[suspenseful music playing]

357
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:08,934
Hey, how are the worms there?

358
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,727
Are they disgusting?

359
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:13,855
I bet it must be so fun
being around them, right?

360
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,233
[laughs]

361
00:21:16,316 --> 00:21:17,943
Hey, come on.

362
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:20,737
Why aren't you answering me?

363
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:25,534
So rude. Hello?

364
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,078
<i>Ivy? Say something.</i>

365
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:31,039
You're always so mad at me.

366
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,749
Now you don't want to answer me.

367
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,751
Mark my words, Emilia.

368
00:21:35,627 --> 00:21:37,045
<i>If I die…</i>

369
00:21:37,129 --> 00:21:38,672
I will haunt you.

370
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:41,049
That is so scary. Don't do that, okay?

371
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:43,385
Why are you so mad at me?

372
00:21:43,468 --> 00:21:46,179
When, in fact, I'm doing you a favor.

373
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:48,181
<i>I'm entertaining you. Because, you know…</i>

374
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:51,685
you must be so bored there in that coffin.

375
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:54,104
Boring, right? [chuckles]

376
00:21:54,187 --> 00:21:56,231
But the truth of the matter is…

377
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,358
um, time has passed.

378
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:01,820
<i>And based on my calculations,</i>
<i>you've only got, like,</i>

379
00:22:01,903 --> 00:22:06,658
three and a half hours left
before you run out of oxygen.

380
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,327
[Emilia] Aw…

381
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:10,120
Poor you.

382
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:12,205
<i>Can you survive that?</i>

383
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:15,709
Well, anyway, I wish you all the best,

384
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,294
<i>and good luck.</i>

385
00:22:17,377 --> 00:22:21,965
And by the way, timer starts now.

386
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:25,761
Tick-tock. Tick-tock.

387
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:28,889
[laughs maniacally]

388
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:29,931
Bye.

389
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:32,601
[ominous music playing]

390
00:22:34,936 --> 00:22:37,647
[panting]

391
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:40,650
[tense music playing]

392
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,664
Oh, okay.

393
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:57,459
[tense music continues]

394
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:02,255
Jaguar.

395
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:03,590
Um, I'm really sorry.

396
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:06,676
But, you know, I have to
reset our date tonight.

397
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,804
Because I just got a phone call from Papa,

398
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:11,056
and he's asking me to do something.

399
00:23:11,139 --> 00:23:14,267
So, let's reschedule
our drinking session, okay?

400
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:15,977
And I shall see you soon.

401
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,980
Bye, Jaguar. I'll see you soon.

402
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,691
[ominous music playing]

403
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:43,964
[phone rings]

404
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:46,758
-Hello, Dad.
-[Raul] <i>Diego, son.</i>

405
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,927
Ivy Aguas is in danger.

406
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:50,762
The Ardientes buried her alive.

407
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:54,224
What? Dad, where is she?

408
00:23:55,433 --> 00:23:57,269
I don't know, son. I didn't ask Emilia.

409
00:23:57,352 --> 00:23:59,187
I don't want her to get suspicious.

410
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:02,566
<i>What's more important is</i>
<i>you have to find and save her.</i>

411
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:03,859
<i>You need to find her.</i>

412
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:05,944
She only has a few hours left.

413
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:08,989
[tense music playing]

414
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:11,908
Diego, what did they do to Ivy?

415
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:19,875
Tell us! What happened to her?

416
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:22,627
[tense music continues]

417
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:45,817
[dramatic music playing]

418
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:16,473
[dramatic continues]

419
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:24,022
[Ivy] <i>As long as you're all there for me,</i>

420
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,775
<i>I won't lose hope.</i>

421
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:30,111
<i>I draw strength from you all.</i>

422
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:34,658
<i>You are the reason why</i>
<i>I will fight to survive.</i>

423
00:25:35,533 --> 00:25:37,535
<i>Why I believe in miracles.</i>

424
00:25:41,206 --> 00:25:42,249
[no audible dialogue]

425
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:45,168
-Good evening, everyone.
-Good evening, Governor.

426
00:25:45,252 --> 00:25:46,753
-Good evening.
-Hello, Chairman.

427
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:48,922
Good evening, everyone.

428
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:52,050
Good evening. I'm glad
you could all make it here.

429
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:55,595
This is for the centennial celebration

430
00:25:55,679 --> 00:25:57,806
of Poblacion Ardiente.

431
00:25:57,889 --> 00:26:00,600
Inform everyone in your districts.

432
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:04,437
Tell them we've prepared
a lot of surprises

433
00:26:04,521 --> 00:26:07,816
and tons of prizes.

434
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:12,737
We're doing this for all the
people of Poblacion Ardiente,

435
00:26:12,821 --> 00:26:15,240
whom I regard as my children.

436
00:26:15,323 --> 00:26:17,575
Friends, I hope to see you there.

437
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:19,452
Papa had this planned out.

438
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:21,830
It's going to be a big celebration.

439
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:23,873
Ardientes!

440
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:29,170
Oh, Diego, Diego.

441
00:26:29,254 --> 00:26:32,465
How are you, my illegitimate grandson?

442
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:34,175
Good thing you came.

443
00:26:34,259 --> 00:26:35,760
Uh, Colonel.

444
00:26:35,844 --> 00:26:38,346
You're invited to the
anniversary of the foundation

445
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:41,182
of our beloved Poblacion Ardiente.

446
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:46,688
I'm not interested in your shenanigans.

447
00:26:48,982 --> 00:26:50,275
Where is Ivy Aguas?

448
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:53,236
Bring her out!

449
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:56,197
[tense music playing]

450
00:26:59,617 --> 00:27:05,582
Diego, why do you care
about Miss Ivy Aguas?

451
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:07,667
Diego, please.

452
00:27:07,751 --> 00:27:10,378
Why are you asking us for Ivy?

453
00:27:10,462 --> 00:27:13,048
Are you accusing us of hiding her?

454
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:14,632
How in the world can we do that

455
00:27:14,716 --> 00:27:16,760
when in fact, we're allies?

456
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:18,636
Honestly, Diego.

457
00:27:19,679 --> 00:27:21,264
You know what, lad?

458
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:25,894
To prove that we have
no bad intentions or whatever,

459
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:28,938
we'll help you find Miss Ivy Aguas.

460
00:27:29,022 --> 00:27:32,233
Colonel, tell your men to get ready.

461
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:37,447
We'll mount an extensive search operation

462
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:39,866
to find Miss Ivy Aguas.

463
00:27:39,949 --> 00:27:41,201
You liar!

464
00:27:41,659 --> 00:27:43,036
[Emilia] Oh, my…

465
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:44,245
Hey.

466
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:48,166
If you did something terrible
to Ivy Aguas,

467
00:27:48,249 --> 00:27:50,001
I'll give you war.

468
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,921
I swear to you, there's going to be war!

469
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:56,966
He thinks we're capable
of doing something that bad.

470
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:58,051
I--

471
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:00,720
Diego, calm down.

472
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:02,639
Where did you bury Ivy Aguas?

473
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:04,891
[tense music playing]

474
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:05,850
[sighs]

475
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:17,320
[sobbing]

476
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:26,121
They're all monsters! All of them!

477
00:28:26,454 --> 00:28:29,582
-All of them! Demons!
-[glass breaking]

478
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:31,668
[sobs]

479
00:28:31,751 --> 00:28:33,336
They buried her alive

480
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:35,505
just like they did to me before!

481
00:28:35,588 --> 00:28:38,800
Now, my daughter too! Bastards!

482
00:28:38,883 --> 00:28:41,177
You demons!

483
00:28:41,261 --> 00:28:43,888
[somber music playing]

484
00:28:46,349 --> 00:28:48,309
[sobbing]

485
00:28:50,937 --> 00:28:53,690
Damian, I can't take this anymore!

486
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:57,777
This situation is just too much for me!

487
00:28:59,237 --> 00:29:01,489
I can't act. I can't do anything.

488
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:04,659
I can't help my daughter because I have to

489
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:07,954
protect her identity from the Ardientes!

490
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:10,957
I understand what you're
going through, Camia.

491
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,044
It's like you're trapped

492
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:17,464
because of all the secrets
you have to keep.

493
00:29:20,967 --> 00:29:25,346
I want to be free
from this secret, Damian.

494
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:27,932
[somber music continues]

495
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:29,225
Camia…

496
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:32,061
Don't you ever put your life in danger.

497
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:36,858
Now that I'm here, I'll help you.

498
00:29:38,109 --> 00:29:39,903
I'll search for your daughter.

499
00:29:40,737 --> 00:29:42,363
[sobs]

500
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:49,746
[sobs]

501
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:57,045
Papa, I'm telling you!

502
00:29:57,128 --> 00:30:00,423
Diego and Ivy Aguas are accomplices!

503
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:04,803
They just won't admit it straight up!

504
00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:07,222
Ivy and Diego?

505
00:30:08,765 --> 00:30:10,141
They're nothing.

506
00:30:11,226 --> 00:30:14,562
Because I am the governor.

507
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:19,400
Elected and proclaimed.

508
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:24,572
So, I don't care if they don't
attend the celebration.

509
00:30:25,031 --> 00:30:26,741
While we celebrate,

510
00:30:27,742 --> 00:30:29,661
the rest of them can all die.

511
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:30,662
I don't care.

512
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:32,872
You know, Papa, this is all your fault.

513
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:36,751
If you just listened to me
over your pet, Ivy Aguas,

514
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:38,837
then we wouldn't be having this problem.

515
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:41,172
What is it going to take

516
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:44,259
for you to stop harping about this?

517
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:46,135
Okay. I want a position.

518
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,764
I want to be your vice governor.

519
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:52,809
[tense music playing]

520
00:30:55,395 --> 00:30:58,648
Before that, make sure that Ivy Aguas

521
00:30:58,731 --> 00:31:00,567
can't dig out of her grave.

522
00:31:01,317 --> 00:31:07,782
And bury our enemies' hope
that they still have a savior.

523
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,661
I want you to assure me

524
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:16,583
that everyone's wonder woman is dead!

525
00:31:16,666 --> 00:31:19,377
[tense music continues]

526
00:31:28,344 --> 00:31:29,554
Jepoy is here.

527
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:30,680
[Loring] Jepoy.

528
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:33,057
Diego.

529
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:36,102
What were you thinking, leaving Ivy alone?

530
00:31:36,936 --> 00:31:38,438
Now, tell me where I'm supposed to look

531
00:31:38,521 --> 00:31:39,480
-because of your failure!
-Jepoy…

532
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:41,524
-Jepoy, that's enough! Enough.
-Tell me!

533
00:31:42,901 --> 00:31:44,402
I need your help.

534
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,864
I need everyone's help.

535
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:51,951
Everyone, please spread the news

536
00:31:52,035 --> 00:31:53,870
that Ivy Aguas is missing.

537
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:57,457
We'll scour the entire province,

538
00:31:57,540 --> 00:32:01,210
and we won't stop until we find her.

539
00:32:01,878 --> 00:32:03,254
-Go now.
-Yes.

540
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:06,382
We'll coordinate and spread out.

541
00:32:06,466 --> 00:32:08,384
Calm yourself, Diego. Calm down.

542
00:32:08,968 --> 00:32:10,136
Be careful, Nanny.

543
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:12,972
-[tense music playing]
-[indistinct chatter]

544
00:32:20,146 --> 00:32:23,608
[phone ringing]

545
00:32:24,525 --> 00:32:25,902
[in deep voice] Hello?

546
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:28,279
Hello. [laughs]

547
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:31,491
Hi, snake! It's still Emilia.

548
00:32:31,991 --> 00:32:33,952
<i>Why? Did you call anyone?</i>

549
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:38,373
Mm… Well, I hope not. But even if you did,

550
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,833
there's nothing they can do anyway, right?

551
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:42,752
<i>Aren't you glad</i>

552
00:32:42,835 --> 00:32:46,798
I left that phone inside that casket?

553
00:32:46,881 --> 00:32:49,258
And you have me for company.

554
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:52,053
[ominous music playing]

555
00:32:52,136 --> 00:32:53,680
Did you miss me?

556
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,354
You don't know where she is, Diego?

557
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:02,647
[Anna] Jepoy!

558
00:33:03,231 --> 00:33:04,816
We'll search for her, Jepoy.

559
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,902
The only thing we can do
right now is work together.

560
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:09,529
We need to cooperate.

561
00:33:15,952 --> 00:33:20,123
[phone rings]

562
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:21,457
Hello?

563
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:24,085
Diego, it's me, Ivy.

564
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:26,337
Ivy.

565
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,925
Help me, Diego.
The Ardientes buried me alive.

566
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:35,179
I'm coming, Ivy.
Just tell me where you are.

567
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:36,472
Where are you?

568
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:39,392
[Emilia] <i>You know, Papa,</i>

569
00:33:39,475 --> 00:33:43,312
no matter how hard
Diego looks for Ivy Aguas,

570
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:46,983
he'll fail because, you know, she's dead.

571
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,152
Prove it.

572
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:53,031
-Prove it.
-Okay. Hold on.

573
00:33:53,114 --> 00:33:55,783
[unsettling music playing]

574
00:33:58,036 --> 00:34:00,079
[line busy]

575
00:34:03,916 --> 00:34:06,002
-[line busy]
-What's wrong?

576
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:10,173
[line busy]

577
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:12,550
-Maybe there's no reception.
-What?

578
00:34:14,093 --> 00:34:17,847
Yeah. Could be that.
Or she must be dead, Papa.

579
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:20,516
I don't know. This is so weird.

580
00:34:21,893 --> 00:34:27,106
I don't give a crap
about your many excuses.

581
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:31,569
What I want from you is the assurance

582
00:34:31,652 --> 00:34:37,366
that Ivy Aguas is in that
plywood box, dead or alive.

583
00:34:37,450 --> 00:34:40,870
[tense music playing]

584
00:34:40,953 --> 00:34:42,038
[groans]

585
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:51,881
Diego…

586
00:34:53,966 --> 00:34:55,051
<i>Diego, listen.</i>

587
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:57,637
Listen carefully.

588
00:34:58,012 --> 00:34:59,472
So you can find me.

589
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:01,057
I'm listening, Ivy.

590
00:35:03,851 --> 00:35:04,811
[Diego] <i>Ivy…</i>

591
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:06,938
[exhales]

592
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:08,856
Diego…

593
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:10,358
Ivy, where are you?

594
00:35:12,985 --> 00:35:14,654
Do you remember…

595
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:19,367
the place where they kept Jepoy?

596
00:35:20,326 --> 00:35:22,370
[Ivy breathes raggedly]

597
00:35:24,413 --> 00:35:25,832
From there…

598
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,459
<i>Take a right.</i>

599
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,254
<i>Emilia's car took a right.</i>

600
00:35:36,634 --> 00:35:38,136
Then, head straight.

601
00:35:38,636 --> 00:35:40,847
<i>We went straight for a while.</i>

602
00:35:43,766 --> 00:35:44,809
Then…

603
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:46,686
<i>We hit…</i>

604
00:35:47,562 --> 00:35:49,021
a rough road.

605
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:52,775
[thuds]

606
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,527
<i>After that, we took a left.</i>

607
00:35:57,071 --> 00:35:58,281
Until…

608
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:05,663
<i>I heard church bells and tricycles.</i>

609
00:36:05,746 --> 00:36:07,707
[breathing raggedly]

610
00:36:08,332 --> 00:36:09,792
There, Diego.

611
00:36:10,334 --> 00:36:12,253
<i>We entered somewhere.</i>

612
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:15,756
<i>That's where they buried me.</i>

613
00:36:16,757 --> 00:36:19,010
There. There, Diego.

614
00:36:19,343 --> 00:36:23,097
I'll save you, Ivy.
Promise me you'll hold on.

615
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:25,433
Promise me you won't give up.

616
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:29,020
I'll hold on.

617
00:36:30,938 --> 00:36:32,315
I'll hold on.

618
00:36:33,107 --> 00:36:35,651
I'll… I'll hold on, Diego.

619
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:38,237
[somber music playing]

620
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:39,655
I'll hold on…

621
00:36:40,948 --> 00:36:42,783
and I'll wait for you.

622
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:46,287
[breathes raggedly]
I'll wait for you, Diego.

623
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:52,960
-I know where Ivy is.
-Where is she?

624
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:54,378
I'm sure there'll be
plenty of guards there.

625
00:36:54,462 --> 00:36:57,131
To pull this off, I'm going
to need your help, Jepoy.

626
00:37:02,762 --> 00:37:04,013
I'll get some help.

627
00:37:04,972 --> 00:37:07,016
You better make sure this works.

628
00:37:07,099 --> 00:37:10,144
[tense music playing]

629
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:25,451
Come on. Pick up the damn phone.

630
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:26,786
[line busy]

631
00:37:26,869 --> 00:37:27,703
[sighs]

632
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:31,707
[line busy]

633
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:33,668
[screams angrily]

634
00:37:34,627 --> 00:37:35,795
[door opens]

635
00:37:35,878 --> 00:37:38,297
Emilia, what's wrong this time?

636
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:40,049
Why are you furious? Just relax.

637
00:37:40,132 --> 00:37:44,053
Don't you tell me to relax.
I'm so stressed right now.

638
00:37:44,136 --> 00:37:46,597
Emilia, I'm here. I'll listen.
What's the problem?

639
00:37:46,681 --> 00:37:47,765
Wow!

640
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:50,142
When did you ever listen to me?

641
00:37:50,226 --> 00:37:51,560
-[scoffs]
-Do you remember, Raul?

642
00:37:51,644 --> 00:37:53,479
You didn't even visit me in prison.

643
00:37:53,562 --> 00:37:56,107
Emilia, I don't have to
tell you what I did.

644
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:58,484
But the day you were imprisoned,

645
00:37:58,567 --> 00:37:59,902
I did what I could.

646
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:01,654
Wow! Really? How sweet.

647
00:38:01,737 --> 00:38:03,656
I don't care anymore, Raul.

648
00:38:03,739 --> 00:38:06,784
I'm very busy preparing for
the celebration of our centennial,

649
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:09,036
and I'm very busy making sure that

650
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:12,373
Ivy Aguas will die tonight.

651
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:15,251
Yes, you heard it right.

652
00:38:15,751 --> 00:38:18,921
She is going to die tonight,
and you're going to help me.

653
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,507
But you know what, Raul?

654
00:38:22,049 --> 00:38:22,925
Don't do anything.

655
00:38:23,009 --> 00:38:26,387
I just realized that Ivy's accomplice,

656
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:28,180
Diego Torillo, is your son.

657
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:30,850
So actually, don't do anything.

658
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:32,643
[scoffs] Seriously, Emilia?

659
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:37,773
You still don't trust me
and my loyalty to you?

660
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:40,818
[tense music playing]

661
00:38:42,445 --> 00:38:45,489
Emilia, I know you're very tired.

662
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:46,782
You're too stressed.

663
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:50,661
Come here. Stay here.

664
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:56,625
What's the problem? Huh?

665
00:38:59,879 --> 00:39:01,255
Rest for a bit.

666
00:39:02,423 --> 00:39:03,716
Let's put that here.

667
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:07,887
Do you want to go on a vacation?

668
00:39:08,471 --> 00:39:09,472
Huh?

669
00:39:09,972 --> 00:39:10,973
[sighs]

670
00:39:11,891 --> 00:39:13,142
Emilia…

671
00:39:15,186 --> 00:39:16,145
Hey.

672
00:39:16,228 --> 00:39:18,856
[unsettling music playing]

673
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:26,155
[solemn music playing]

674
00:39:26,238 --> 00:39:28,199
[Ivy] <i>I have to get out of here.</i>

675
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:32,411
<i>For the people.</i>

676
00:39:33,954 --> 00:39:35,331
<i>For justice.</i>

677
00:39:37,458 --> 00:39:38,876
<i>For my mother.</i>

678
00:39:38,959 --> 00:39:41,670
[solemn music continues]

679
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:42,963
[exhales]

680
00:39:45,257 --> 00:39:46,258
[exhales]

681
00:39:48,219 --> 00:39:49,220
Ivy…

682
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:53,224
Ivy, hang on.

683
00:39:57,436 --> 00:39:58,854
Hang on, Ivy.

684
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:04,235
[line rings]

685
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:08,447
[Anna] He's not picking up, Miss Loring.

686
00:40:09,031 --> 00:40:10,741
I'll try calling Jepoy.

687
00:40:12,118 --> 00:40:13,452
[line rings]

688
00:40:15,162 --> 00:40:17,081
[Anna] He's not picking up, either.

689
00:40:17,665 --> 00:40:21,377
-[line continues ringing]
-[Loring] Where are they?

690
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:22,670
Where could they be?

691
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:25,214
[Anna] Their phones just keep ringing.

692
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:30,970
Miss Camia, Diego and Jepoy
aren't picking up yet.

693
00:40:31,345 --> 00:40:33,597
We have to go, with or without them.

694
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:35,182
Hold on.

695
00:40:35,266 --> 00:40:37,893
We don't even know where Ivy is.

696
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:39,603
Where are we going
to start looking for her?

697
00:40:39,687 --> 00:40:41,021
Miss Loring,

698
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:43,107
what matters is that we do something.

699
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:46,902
Every second we waste brings
Ivy closer to death's door.

700
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:50,489
[tense music playing]

701
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:55,703
Cheers!

702
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,872
Bottles everywhere!

703
00:40:58,289 --> 00:41:01,375
What is this place, a rest house?!

704
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,127
Boss Jaguar, you're alive!

705
00:41:03,752 --> 00:41:05,337
Do I look dead to you?

706
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:08,716
[laughs mockingly]

707
00:41:08,799 --> 00:41:11,427
-Can a ghost do that?
-Why me, Boss?

708
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:14,930
Remember, cats have nine lives.

709
00:41:15,681 --> 00:41:17,433
I won't die that easily.

710
00:41:17,808 --> 00:41:20,644
-Long live Boss Jaguar!
-To the boss!

711
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,563
[laughs]

712
00:41:22,646 --> 00:41:23,939
Stop that!

713
00:41:26,192 --> 00:41:28,819
Get your guns.
We're going on a field trip.

714
00:41:30,738 --> 00:41:32,031
-Let's go.
-Move it!

715
00:41:32,114 --> 00:41:34,283
[ominous music playing]

716
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:36,994
[grunts]

717
00:41:37,828 --> 00:41:39,788
-Did any of you wear this?!
-Mallari did!

718
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:41,916
Mallari, you're dead meat!

719
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:45,461
[ominous music continues]

720
00:41:58,766 --> 00:42:01,227
[laughs mockingly]

721
00:42:05,105 --> 00:42:07,983
[tense music playing]

722
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:11,445
[handbrake clicks]

723
00:42:22,289 --> 00:42:24,041
-[line rings]
-Jepoy, where are you?

724
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:25,751
We're about to leave.

725
00:42:25,834 --> 00:42:26,919
[Jepoy] <i>Anna, listen to me.</i>

726
00:42:27,253 --> 00:42:29,171
Diego knows where they buried Ivy.

727
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:30,673
He's with Arthur right now.

728
00:42:30,756 --> 00:42:32,174
And you? Where are you going?

729
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:34,635
I've got another plan.

730
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:36,887
I'm looking for help.

731
00:42:36,971 --> 00:42:39,139
We're going to help. We're going to Lily.

732
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:40,975
-You can't.
-What do you mean, we can't?

733
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:44,436
I can't just sit here
while my friends need help.

734
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:46,021
<i>Anna, listen to me.</i>

735
00:42:46,105 --> 00:42:49,858
I know and understand that
we're all worried for Ivy.

736
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,610
<i>But it's suicide to…</i>

737
00:42:51,694 --> 00:42:54,822
barge into enemy territory
without any weapons or backup.

738
00:42:55,447 --> 00:42:56,365
You're safer at the headquarters.

739
00:42:56,448 --> 00:42:58,033
<i>Just stay there. Don't leave.</i>

740
00:42:58,367 --> 00:42:59,243
But, Jepoy…

741
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,328
<i>Just do as I say, Anna.</i>

742
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:03,455
If Ivy were here, she'd tell you that too.

743
00:43:03,539 --> 00:43:04,957
I hope you get where I'm coming from.

744
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:07,960
[tense music continues]

745
00:43:09,837 --> 00:43:10,879
[exhales]

746
00:43:19,221 --> 00:43:20,764
[knocking on gate]

747
00:43:27,855 --> 00:43:28,897
Anna…

748
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:31,358
Diego's on his way to Lily, Auntie Camia.

749
00:43:31,859 --> 00:43:33,444
Jepoy's going to help too.

750
00:43:33,861 --> 00:43:36,780
So, please don't worry.
Lily's going to be safe.

751
00:43:37,239 --> 00:43:38,824
I understand that, Anna.

752
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:42,036
I know Diego won't let anything happen

753
00:43:42,119 --> 00:43:43,329
to my daughter.

754
00:43:43,412 --> 00:43:44,455
They won't.

755
00:43:44,538 --> 00:43:49,168
I believe that they'll find
and rescue my Lily.

756
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:52,254
[somber music playing]

757
00:43:58,010 --> 00:44:01,013
[suspenseful music playing]

758
00:44:03,557 --> 00:44:05,267
[Ivy] <i>Do you remember</i>

759
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:08,187
<i>the place where they kept Jepoy?</i>

760
00:44:09,271 --> 00:44:11,815
<i>From there, take a right.</i>

761
00:44:12,441 --> 00:44:13,525
Turn right.

762
00:44:20,991 --> 00:44:22,409
[Ivy] <i>Head straight.</i>

763
00:44:23,994 --> 00:44:26,246
[Ivy] <i>We went straight for a while.</i>

764
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:28,499
Just keep going straight.

765
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:34,004
Ivy, hold on.

766
00:44:35,756 --> 00:44:37,508
Don't give up, Ivy.

767
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:40,052
[honks]

768
00:44:44,223 --> 00:44:48,018
[Ivy] <i>Then, we hit a rough road.</i>

769
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:52,022
Diego, are we still on the right path?

770
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:53,899
We're going to pass through a rough road.

771
00:44:53,982 --> 00:44:55,359
That's what Ivy told me.

772
00:44:58,237 --> 00:45:01,365
[suspenseful music playing]

773
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,287
This is it.

774
00:45:10,499 --> 00:45:12,459
[Ivy] After that, we took a left.

775
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:16,547
Turn left after the rough road.

776
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,887
[suspenseful music continues]

777
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:31,186
[Ivy] <i>Until I heard</i>
<i>church bells and tricycles.</i>

778
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:38,360
[church bell tolls]

779
00:45:39,611 --> 00:45:41,822
Get ready. We're almost there.

780
00:45:47,619 --> 00:45:48,996
You need to relax.

781
00:45:52,958 --> 00:45:55,794
[unsettling music playing]

782
00:45:55,878 --> 00:45:57,880
I'll get you a cup of tea, okay?

783
00:45:57,963 --> 00:45:59,590
It'll help you relax.

784
00:46:00,048 --> 00:46:01,175
Thank you.

785
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:07,598
[door closes]

786
00:46:14,313 --> 00:46:15,564
[line rings]

787
00:46:15,647 --> 00:46:17,065
Hello, Domingo.

788
00:46:17,149 --> 00:46:21,445
Make sure no one comes near
Ivy Aguas' grave, okay?

789
00:46:21,528 --> 00:46:23,906
I don't care if you have to
guard it for an hour

790
00:46:23,989 --> 00:46:25,157
or a year.

791
00:46:25,240 --> 00:46:27,659
Shoot anyone who approaches her grave.

792
00:46:30,746 --> 00:46:31,997
Understood?

793
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:33,582
Good.

794
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:36,668
[ominous music playing]

795
00:46:51,141 --> 00:46:54,102
[ominous music swelling]

796
00:47:09,826 --> 00:47:10,994
[handbrake clicks]

797
00:47:11,912 --> 00:47:13,163
We're here.

798
00:47:14,248 --> 00:47:15,207
Let's go.

799
00:47:15,290 --> 00:47:17,876
[unsettling music playing]

800
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:26,885
Ivy's here somewhere.

801
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:30,973
If we have to dig up every grave,
so be it.

802
00:47:31,056 --> 00:47:32,057
As long as we find her.

803
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:34,309
We have to find her, understood?

804
00:47:34,393 --> 00:47:36,270
Arthur, search that area.
Batch, go that way.

805
00:47:36,353 --> 00:47:37,437
Okay.

806
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:39,398
Wait, Diego! Wait!

807
00:47:40,232 --> 00:47:41,942
[goon 1] The Ardientes are slave drivers.

808
00:47:42,025 --> 00:47:44,236
They want us to guard
a cemetery at this hour?

809
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:45,946
What are we supposed to shoot? Zombies?

810
00:47:46,029 --> 00:47:49,533
[goon 2] Stop complaining.
You're getting paid anyway.

811
00:47:49,616 --> 00:47:51,034
We need to move.

812
00:47:51,118 --> 00:47:53,078
We can't just charge them.

813
00:47:53,161 --> 00:47:54,580
We don't have time.

814
00:47:54,663 --> 00:47:57,207
Ivy's going to run out of air!
Do you understand?

815
00:47:57,291 --> 00:47:58,417
-Let's go.
-Wait!

816
00:47:58,500 --> 00:47:59,876
What if they gun us down?!

817
00:47:59,960 --> 00:48:02,879
[tense music playing]

818
00:48:05,507 --> 00:48:07,050
All right, you stay here.

819
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:08,260
[goon 2] Stay put.

820
00:48:09,678 --> 00:48:10,721
[goon 3] Guard this area.

821
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:14,141
[tense music continues]

822
00:48:14,224 --> 00:48:16,518
[breathes heavily]

823
00:48:21,106 --> 00:48:22,399
Please answer.

824
00:48:22,482 --> 00:48:26,320
[phone rings]

825
00:48:35,787 --> 00:48:37,789
Ivy… Ivy, we're here.

826
00:48:39,583 --> 00:48:42,210
Don't worry. We'll save you.

827
00:48:43,587 --> 00:48:45,339
<i>Just hold on.</i>

828
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:47,883
[tense music playing]

829
00:48:59,686 --> 00:49:01,855
<i>Lily's been through so much.</i>

830
00:49:01,938 --> 00:49:04,024
<i>This won't take her down.</i>

831
00:49:04,107 --> 00:49:05,025
<i>You're going to die.</i>

832
00:49:05,108 --> 00:49:07,736
<i>Oh, poor, Ivy.</i>

833
00:49:07,819 --> 00:49:10,113
<i>I'm Ivy Aguas.</i>

834
00:49:10,197 --> 00:49:12,783
<i>I can handle everything.</i>

835
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:14,576
[Emilia chuckles]

836
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:16,536
<i>-Hello, Dad.</i>
<i>-Where are you? I'll help you.</i>

837
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:19,247
<i>We're going to save Ivy</i>
<i>no matter what happens.</i>

838
00:49:19,331 --> 00:49:22,876
[Damian] <i>I'm here to help Ivy Aguas.</i>

839
00:49:22,959 --> 00:49:24,294
[rapid gunfire]

840
00:49:26,213 --> 00:49:29,466
[Camia] <i>She still has to bring</i>
<i>those criminals to justice.</i>
